"A1 iteration 7 is finished with one general engine change, now engine `e3-1.9.0`. It improves angle accuracy where real bends are rounder than the CAD says. Gate verdicts are unchanged: G2 still fails (a) and (f), and G3 still fails. The synthetic regression tier passes as before, the 169 engine tests pass, and the change record is written.\n\n**Start state.** The snapshot `engine_before.tgz` (sha `160a0e79\u2026`) was already there and the engine matched it byte for byte, so I kept it. Iteration 6 did not regress and its generality check was clean, so nothing was reverted or removed.\n\n**Your question from the E2E audit (10839000 FULL angles at 88.0\u201389.7\u00b0): this is the part's real shape, not an engine bias.** I checked it with cross-section profiles of the scan:\n- The two 12 mm lips are flat and overbent: their flat portions stand at 88.2\u201388.7\u00b0.\n- The base is tilted 0.7\u20131.8\u00b0 near the middle of its long edges, while the walls are flat. Measured against the base's average plane, the walls stand at 89.1\u201389.6\u00b0.\n- On scan_2, the same engine reads B5/B7/B10/B12 within 0.43\u00b0 of nominal, so it is not a systematic bias.\n- I did not change the engine to hide the bow. As a result, the G3 known-good angle gate cannot pass on this part with an honest local measurement. **Decision for you:** keep 10839000 as \"known-good at \u00b11\u00b0\", or score that gate against the base's average plane.\n\n**The change: each side's measuring window now starts on that side's own flat material.**\n- Before, the window started 0.5 mm past where the CAD radius ends. Real bends often keep curving beyond that point; on 15651004 the real inner radius is about 2.6 mm against 0.8 mm in the CAD.\n- That curved tail pushed angles toward reading underbent and spread the readings along the bend.\n- The engine now steps outward until a short strip lines up with the straight sheet beyond it. If no flat strip is found within 4 mm, it keeps the old start.\n- The rule uses only the scan's own surface; there is no part- or family-specific logic. There are seven new config fields, all range-checked; no gate threshold changed.\n\n**Results on the 26 runnable real cases** (159 measured angles, the two wrong-way hooks excluded):\n\n| Measure | Iteration 6 | Iteration 7 |\n|---|---|---|\n| Angle error vs nominal (mean) | 0.946\u00b0 | 0.898\u00b0 |\n| Angle uncertainty (mean) | 1.018\u00b0 | 0.956\u00b0 |\n| 15651004 angle error | 0.698\u00b0 | 0.364\u00b0 |\n| 23553000 angle error | 1.002\u00b0 | 0.788\u00b0 |\n| G2(c) known-good angle (passes, limit 1.0\u00b0) | 0.795\u00b0 | 0.798\u00b0 |\n| G2(f) repeatability (limit 0.3\u00b0) | 0.426\u00b0 | 0.306\u00b0 |\n| G3 known-good angle (limit 1.0\u00b0) | 1.186\u00b0 | 1.147\u00b0 |\n\n- G2(f) still fails, and its three 15651004 \"repeat\" scans are really three different stages.\n- G3 still fails because of 10839000, as above.\n- Line-matching scores, GOLD_SET_V1, the Gold11 relabel and per-bend correctness (183/203 = 0.901, 3 suspected false PASSes, the same bends) are unchanged.\n- Decision changes: 5 angles went REVIEW\u2192PASS and 3 went PASS\u2192REVIEW. 3 went REVIEW\u2192FAIL; their readings now agree along the bend, and traces show a clean curved tail on each, but there is no physical truth for them.\n\n**Checks** (all run one at a time under the shared lock):\n- Synthetic regression tier: PASS, with 29 of 32 gate records identical to iteration 6; the other 3 are timing only.\n- CAD-stage probes: 113 probes, every aggregate identical to iteration 6; 3 of 503 angles moved, by at most 0.05\u00b0.\n- Tests: 19 new tests pass; the full engine test set passes, 169 tests.\n- After a final small safeguard in the fitting code, I re-ran the real cases, the synthetic tier and the tests: every result was identical.\n\n**Not changed:**\n- **Joggle angles:** they stay REVIEW with \u00b17\u20138\u00b0 uncertainty, because the joggle's middle section has no flat material to measure.\n- **Part summary's \"worst\" item:** a high-uncertainty REVIEW can outrank a clear FAIL there. That ranking lives in `contracts/production/inspection_result.py`, which A1 does not own. I suggest ranking FAIL first, then REVIEW.\n- **Same search at the far end next to an adjacent bend:** I tried it and did not keep it. It worsened one bend by mistaking a small dip in the surface for a curved tail; it is a candidate for iteration 8.\n- **Tab-merge false positives on 38172000 SCAN_1:** still waiting on your labelling decision.\n- **Fold the recipe excludes on 28870000 FULL:** there is no recipe row to report it on.\n- **Rolled 28870000 SCAN_1:** loosening the wrong-part check would risk wrong or mirrored parts passing.\n- **Thickness spread between scans:** the measured thickness varies between scans; left as is.\n\nFiles are in `/Users/idantal/ShermanQC/FullProject/docs/production/runlog/a1/iter_7/`:\n- CHANGE.md\n- engine.diff\n- diag/\n- validation/\n- tools/\n\nThe new tests are in `/Users/idantal/ShermanQC/FullProject/tests/test_prod_engine_inspect_a1_iter7.py`."